= Taxonomy — Simple =

A '''taxonomy''' is an organized set of categories or concepts.

It often looks like a hierarchy:

<pre>
Animal
→ Mammal
→ Dog
</pre>

Taxonomies help people:
* browse information;
* classify things;
* find related concepts;
* use consistent names.

A taxonomy is not the same as an [[Ontology/Simple|ontology]].

A taxonomy is usually focused on organizing categories.

An ontology can describe many kinds of relationships and formal rules.

A taxonomy can also have more than one parent for a concept. For example, Bioinformatics can belong under both Biology and Computer science.

